Devices:
2 PCs, 1 Switch, 1 Server, 1 Printer

IP:
PC0 = 192.168.1.10 /24
PC1 = 192.168.1.20 /24
Server = 192.168.1.100 /24
Printer = 192.168.1.50 /24

Server -> Services -> FTP -> On.
Create an FTP username and password.

From PC Command Prompt:
ftp 192.168.1.100
dir
get filename
put filename
quit

Test:
ping 192.168.1.50

Save:
Exp8_LAN_FTP_Printer.pkt
Compile / Run:
Use Cisco Packet Tracer.
Sample Output:
PC0> ftp 192.168.1.100
Connected to 192.168.1.100.
Name: student
Password: ****
ftp> dir
ftp> get test.txt
ftp> quit

PC0> ping 192.168.1.50
Reply from 192.168.1.50: bytes=32 time<1ms TTL=128
